1
00:00:06,466 --> 00:00:07,626
SCENES FROM THE PREVIOUS EPISODE

2
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:10,010
<i>Hello? Yes, this is she.</i>

3
00:00:10,094 --> 00:00:11,644
<i>All right, see you soon.</i>

4
00:00:12,055 --> 00:00:13,675
I have a job interview!

5
00:00:14,474 --> 00:00:17,444
When my father finds out
I'm interviewing to be a secretary,

6
00:00:17,727 --> 00:00:18,727
he'll say,

7
00:00:18,811 --> 00:00:21,731
"Betty, that's not what
you went to college for!"

8
00:00:21,814 --> 00:00:24,364
<i>But if I'm offered the job, I'm taking it.</i>

9
00:00:24,609 --> 00:00:26,069
<i>I'll figure out what to tell him later.</i>

10
00:00:26,152 --> 00:00:27,032
Silence!

11
00:00:27,111 --> 00:00:29,781
Mine is the only voice
we should be hearing.

12
00:00:30,949 --> 00:00:33,029
I'm looking for Human Resources.

13
00:00:33,117 --> 00:00:34,367
Oh, the horror!

14
00:00:34,452 --> 00:00:36,452
That's a very impressive résumé.

15
00:00:36,579 --> 00:00:38,499
Why do you want to be a secretary?

16
00:00:38,581 --> 00:00:42,341
I feel like there's tremendous opportunity
for growth at VandM.

17
00:00:43,503 --> 00:00:47,013
I'm Patricia Fernandez, Marcela's friend.

18
00:00:47,131 --> 00:00:50,261
<i>The one who's applying to be</i>
<i>the president's secretary.</i>

19
00:00:50,343 --> 00:00:51,973
Will you marry me?

20
00:00:52,053 --> 00:00:54,353
Armando proposed to secure
your vote and become president,

21
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,310
that's all.

22
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:57,480
Armando and I have been together
more than two years.

23
00:00:57,559 --> 00:00:58,429
<i>We're in love.</i>

24
00:00:58,810 --> 00:01:00,940
-You sure there's nobody here?
-Nobody!

25
00:01:01,187 --> 00:01:02,687
If Marcela sees us, she'll kill us.

26
00:01:06,818 --> 00:01:07,648
Who's there?

27
00:01:07,735 --> 00:01:10,195
Get out right now! No, don't!

28
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:12,620
You can come out now.
What are you doing here?

29
00:01:13,491 --> 00:01:14,911
Open up!

30
00:01:14,993 --> 00:01:16,373
Armando, I know you're in there!

31
00:01:16,452 --> 00:01:21,122
Don't make me call security! Armando!

32
00:01:22,709 --> 00:01:24,039
Armando!

33
00:01:24,627 --> 00:01:26,047
Where's Armando?

34
00:01:26,379 --> 00:01:28,549
This young lady and I
are the only ones in here.

35
00:01:28,631 --> 00:01:30,801
Was there a man here?

36
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:31,723
No.

37
00:01:31,801 --> 00:01:32,641
Where were you?

38
00:01:32,719 --> 00:01:35,509
What's wrong? Why are you upset?
What'd I do?

39
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:37,636
Patricia is going to be
your new secretary.

40
00:01:37,724 --> 00:01:40,484
What made you think Patricia Fernandez
could be my secretary?

41
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:43,270
There's another candidate.
She's actually overqualified.

42
00:01:43,354 --> 00:01:45,064
That's who I want.

43
00:01:45,148 --> 00:01:46,018
She's ugly.

44
00:01:46,107 --> 00:01:47,227
How ugly can she be?

45
00:01:47,317 --> 00:01:49,737
Mr. Mendoza, the other candidate is here.

46
00:01:49,819 --> 00:01:50,819
Send her in.

47
00:01:50,903 --> 00:01:53,363
Ms. Beatriz Aurora Rincon.

48
00:01:54,407 --> 00:01:55,277
You?

49
00:01:55,908 --> 00:01:56,738
You?

50
00:01:58,786 --> 00:01:59,946
Thank you, Smith.

51
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,040
You know each other?

52
00:02:02,582 --> 00:02:05,382
No, of course not.
This is the first time we've met.

53
00:02:06,753 --> 00:02:09,843
This is your résumé?

54
00:02:09,922 --> 00:02:11,722
Pleased to meet you.

55
00:02:12,216 --> 00:02:15,426
You were in the restroom
with Naomi, weren't you?

56
00:02:15,511 --> 00:02:16,761
How do you know her?

57
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:18,100
I don't.

58
00:02:18,181 --> 00:02:19,771
We just ran into each other
in the restroom.

59
00:02:19,849 --> 00:02:21,479
Hello. How is everyone?

60
00:02:21,559 --> 00:02:22,809
Hi, Dad.

61
00:02:23,102 --> 00:02:26,362
I haven't left yet, and you've
already changed the decor.

62
00:02:26,439 --> 00:02:28,939
You're changing many things, huh?

63
00:02:30,401 --> 00:02:31,611
And this young lady is?

64
00:02:31,694 --> 00:02:32,784
My new secretary.

65
00:02:32,862 --> 00:02:35,572
No, we're in the process
of selecting his new secretary.

66
00:02:36,407 --> 00:02:38,787
Why don't you stay and help us?

67
00:02:39,035 --> 00:02:44,205
I don't need anyone's help
choosing my own secretary, dear.

68
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:47,670
Why is she in there, and I'm not?

69
00:02:48,044 --> 00:02:50,964
The job was mine. You said so.

70
00:02:51,047 --> 00:02:52,127
Why'd you bring her?

71
00:02:52,715 --> 00:02:56,385
Ms. Fernandez, to Ms. Valencia and I,

72
00:02:56,469 --> 00:02:58,219
you are the ideal candidate,

73
00:02:58,304 --> 00:03:03,184
but the president wanted
to interview that... young lady.

74
00:03:03,267 --> 00:03:05,347
That loser?

75
00:03:05,770 --> 00:03:09,150
How can someone like her
take my job from me?

76
00:03:09,232 --> 00:03:10,982
I mean, look at her!

77
00:03:11,317 --> 00:03:16,737
She has none of my class,
elegance or presence.

78
00:03:18,074 --> 00:03:18,954
Right, Ricky?

79
00:03:21,285 --> 00:03:23,745
Apples and oranges.

80
00:03:24,372 --> 00:03:25,252
I mean,

81
00:03:25,331 --> 00:03:27,331
what's so special about her?

82
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:33,880
Oh, well, only that she graduated
Summa Cum Laude

83
00:03:34,173 --> 00:03:35,633
with two post-graduate degrees,

84
00:03:35,717 --> 00:03:38,047
a degree in Finance,
and she speaks five languages but...

85
00:03:38,761 --> 00:03:40,641
-Five?
-Five.

86
00:03:41,514 --> 00:03:43,984
All she's missing is an Olympic medal.

87
00:03:44,058 --> 00:03:47,098
No, there's not an athletic bone
in her body.

88
00:03:47,979 --> 00:03:49,359
-Patricia.
-Yeah?

89
00:03:49,439 --> 00:03:50,689
Please join us.

90
00:03:56,154 --> 00:03:58,784
Patricia, please stand
next to this young lady.

91
00:04:02,577 --> 00:04:03,537
<i>Bonjour.</i>

92
00:04:04,871 --> 00:04:08,291
Roberto, these are our two candidates.

93
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:12,170
Could you wait outside
for a moment, please?

94
00:04:19,469 --> 00:04:21,219
That was low, Marcela.

95
00:04:22,138 --> 00:04:25,098
Dad, Beatriz Rincon is more qualified

96
00:04:25,183 --> 00:04:27,643
than that bimbo Patricia.

97
00:04:27,727 --> 00:04:31,307
Beatriz Aurora Rincon Lozano.
Very interesting.

98
00:04:32,315 --> 00:04:34,895
It's unbelievable how you
could humiliate that poor girl

99
00:04:34,984 --> 00:04:36,324
by making her stand next to your friend.

100
00:04:36,402 --> 00:04:39,612
No, what's unbelievable is you hiring
that insignificant woman

101
00:04:39,697 --> 00:04:42,617
for a job that requires
elegance and social skills.

102
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:44,790
We're a fashion house.

103
00:04:45,036 --> 00:04:47,996
Your secretary should represent
the company.

104
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:49,460
Isn't that right, Roberto?

105
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:51,880
I doubt he'll disregard
someone's skill set

106
00:04:51,959 --> 00:04:54,169
in favor of their image, right, Dad?

107
00:04:54,253 --> 00:04:55,803
You're both right.

108
00:04:56,589 --> 00:05:00,009
Patricia is elegant,
sociable and distinguished.

109
00:05:00,092 --> 00:05:05,352
And this young lady, Beatriz,
has an impressive résumé

110
00:05:05,431 --> 00:05:07,811
and appears to be efficient.

111
00:05:07,934 --> 00:05:12,404
Why not hire them both
on a one-month trial period?

112
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:15,690
You can decide who stays after that.

113
00:05:30,039 --> 00:05:31,249
Hello, Mr. Valencia.

114
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Don't be an idiot.

115
00:05:34,293 --> 00:05:36,003
If you were a spy, you'd be dead.

116
00:05:36,546 --> 00:05:38,086
-What do you have for me?
-Sorry, sir.

117
00:05:39,048 --> 00:05:42,508
This is Mendoza's business plan.

118
00:05:43,010 --> 00:05:45,510
All of its mistakes are underlined in red.

119
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:48,270
If he goes through with the plan,

120
00:05:48,349 --> 00:05:51,229
we'll have serious financial
troubles within six months.

121
00:05:51,310 --> 00:05:53,940
And you know what else?
He won't meet his goal.

122
00:05:54,689 --> 00:05:55,899
Good job, Mata.

123
00:05:56,607 --> 00:05:58,857
I'll present this report
at our next meeting

124
00:05:59,402 --> 00:06:01,032
before Roberto leaves the country.

125
00:06:01,779 --> 00:06:04,659
My sister has to wake up
and see who that man really is.

126
00:06:06,450 --> 00:06:07,410
Don't worry.

127
00:06:07,493 --> 00:06:09,203
Armando is his own worst enemy.

128
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:11,210
The company was very chaotic this morning.

129
00:06:11,289 --> 00:06:13,419
There was so much noise...

130
00:06:13,499 --> 00:06:15,289
Mata! What happened?

131
00:06:16,627 --> 00:06:19,377
I was in the lobby when I noticed
your sister looking very tense.

132
00:06:21,507 --> 00:06:22,877
<i>She was arguing with Wilson.</i>

133
00:06:23,884 --> 00:06:27,224
There's a model locked in the bathroom.

134
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:28,890
I need the keys! Give them to me!

135
00:06:28,973 --> 00:06:30,643
It's the master key.

136
00:06:30,725 --> 00:06:32,515
I'm not authorized to give them to you.

137
00:06:32,602 --> 00:06:33,812
It's an order!

138
00:06:33,894 --> 00:06:37,194
I can go with you to open the door.

139
00:06:37,273 --> 00:06:38,613
Let's go!

140
00:06:40,901 --> 00:06:42,491
<i>I don't know what happened afterward.</i>

141
00:06:43,487 --> 00:06:47,067
She was tense, but also upset,
angry, annoyed...

142
00:06:47,158 --> 00:06:47,988
Mata!

143
00:06:49,452 --> 00:06:52,252
Like when Armando was found
with that model.

144
00:06:52,330 --> 00:06:54,370
Remember her?
That dark, long-haired beauty?

145
00:06:54,457 --> 00:06:56,497
Mata, here's what we'll do:

146
00:06:57,126 --> 00:07:02,006
Find out which model was in the restroom,
and watch Armando.

147
00:07:02,298 --> 00:07:04,298
I'll do some digging of my own.

148
00:07:10,222 --> 00:07:16,062
Marce, thank you for treating me
to a massage.

149
00:07:16,145 --> 00:07:19,685
I really needed it. I'm very stressed out.

150
00:07:19,899 --> 00:07:24,649
I don't know how I'm going to put up
with that scarecrow in the office.

151
00:07:24,737 --> 00:07:26,567
I know. Don't even bring her up.

152
00:07:26,906 --> 00:07:30,366
I don't like that woman. She's dangerous.

153
00:07:30,451 --> 00:07:34,751
Look, don't worry.
Beatriz won't last long at VandM.

154
00:07:35,122 --> 00:07:39,542
I'll take bug spray to work
tomorrow and get rid of her.

155
00:07:42,546 --> 00:07:46,256
But Marce... You know my situation.

156
00:07:46,342 --> 00:07:47,972
Don't start, Patricia.

157
00:07:48,678 --> 00:07:51,218
I already gave you a one-week advance.

158
00:07:52,056 --> 00:07:54,516
And don't you dare
tell the other secretaries

159
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,850
how much you earn,
which is much more than they do.

160
00:07:57,269 --> 00:08:00,479
-I'm not a secretary.
-Whatever.

161
00:08:04,777 --> 00:08:06,817
<i>Hi, Patricia. It's Daniel Valencia.</i>

162
00:08:06,904 --> 00:08:09,914
<i>Let's have dinner.</i>
<i>No one needs to know, you know?</i>

163
00:08:10,533 --> 00:08:13,493
I know that smile. Who is it?

164
00:08:13,577 --> 00:08:14,657
Stop it!

165
00:08:17,248 --> 00:08:18,618
-You won't tell me who it is?
-No.

166
00:08:18,708 --> 00:08:19,668
I have to get ready.

167
00:08:19,875 --> 00:08:21,165
Yes! What do I wear?

168
00:08:21,252 --> 00:08:22,592
Oh, Marce.

169
00:08:25,256 --> 00:08:27,336
-You going to eat that?
-Don't! Of course I am!

170
00:08:27,425 --> 00:08:28,425
You're so stingy!

171
00:08:31,053 --> 00:08:34,063
It's your first time
beating the pretty girl.

172
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:38,350
That calls for a celebration!
Let's get beers or a bottle!

173
00:08:38,978 --> 00:08:42,058
There's nothing to celebrate.
I didn't beat anyone.

174
00:08:42,148 --> 00:08:45,358
We're competing to see who gets the job.

175
00:08:45,901 --> 00:08:48,781
And as always happens, it'll probably be
that Patricia Fernandez.

176
00:08:48,863 --> 00:08:51,453
Quit being so pessimistic.

177
00:08:55,202 --> 00:08:57,122
Send the pessimism away.

178
00:08:58,789 --> 00:09:03,539
If we strip away the glamour,
luxury and the models,

179
00:09:03,627 --> 00:09:08,047
VandM is just a company that needs
to make money to survive.

180
00:09:08,132 --> 00:09:10,842
What are you good at?

181
00:09:12,344 --> 00:09:15,224
Don't make me go deaf, Betty!

182
00:09:15,306 --> 00:09:16,466
Make that your mantra.

183
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:19,060
You have to believe it.

184
00:09:19,477 --> 00:09:21,307
Yes, Betty.

185
00:09:21,395 --> 00:09:23,765
-Know what else gives me hope?
-What?

186
00:09:23,856 --> 00:09:27,276
Mr. Armando, the son of VandM's owner,

187
00:09:28,152 --> 00:09:29,742
defended me in front of his girlfriend.

188
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:33,700
I'm sure he wants me
to stay at the company.

189
00:09:33,783 --> 00:09:36,663
And you will, Betty.

190
00:09:36,744 --> 00:09:38,834
So what's the scoop?

191
00:09:38,913 --> 00:09:42,123
You were in the bathroom
and Naomi was with your boss

192
00:09:42,208 --> 00:09:45,918
and you caught them red-handed?
Please tell me more!

193
00:09:46,003 --> 00:09:47,463
Super red-handed!

194
00:09:49,673 --> 00:09:53,433
I was in the stall,
and Naomi and Armando were outside.

195
00:09:53,511 --> 00:09:54,851
Then his fiancée showed up.

196
00:09:54,929 --> 00:09:58,929
I'm sure Naomi will never
set foot in VandM again.

197
00:09:59,266 --> 00:10:02,766
Why didn't you call or FaceTime me?

198
00:10:02,853 --> 00:10:05,733
I wanted to see her. You know I love her!

199
00:10:05,815 --> 00:10:09,935
She's my Aphrodite!
You're such a bad friend!

200
00:10:10,194 --> 00:10:13,704
Quit acting like
a horny old coot, Nicolas!

201
00:10:13,781 --> 00:10:15,411
"She's my Aphrodite!"

202
00:10:15,658 --> 00:10:18,038
Well, she arouses me. Is that so bad?

203
00:10:18,119 --> 00:10:19,409
Nicolas!

204
00:10:30,506 --> 00:10:32,586
Hello, Armando. How are you?

205
00:10:33,217 --> 00:10:34,087
I'm well.

206
00:10:35,094 --> 00:10:38,354
Does this mean you agree to be part
of my fashion show?

207
00:10:40,015 --> 00:10:42,425
I'm dying to work with Shannon De Lima.

208
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:49,070
Maybe.

209
00:10:54,029 --> 00:10:56,159
Hey, hey. Are you leaving just like that?

210
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:57,410
-Huh?
-Already?

211
00:10:57,491 --> 00:11:00,121
You have my answer. Maybe.

212
00:11:04,874 --> 00:11:07,424
I wanted to congratulate you
on your new job at VandM.

213
00:11:08,002 --> 00:11:10,922
You're Armando Mendoza's
executive secretary.

214
00:11:11,755 --> 00:11:14,375
You really know how to make
the most of your connections.

215
00:11:15,759 --> 00:11:17,509
Thank you, Daniel.

216
00:11:19,263 --> 00:11:22,853
I'm thrilled you asked me out to dinner.

217
00:11:23,559 --> 00:11:27,899
Now we can get to know each other better.

218
00:11:30,107 --> 00:11:32,857
Don't congratulate me just yet, though.

219
00:11:33,193 --> 00:11:36,243
Armando hired another secretary.

220
00:11:36,322 --> 00:11:38,572
He did? Why does he need two?

221
00:11:38,741 --> 00:11:40,451
Is he so inept
he can't manage with just one?

222
00:11:41,493 --> 00:11:42,623
What can I say?

223
00:11:42,703 --> 00:11:44,043
That's Armando for you.

224
00:11:44,872 --> 00:11:47,252
It's obvious he isn't ready
to be president.

225
00:11:47,583 --> 00:11:51,633
Plus, he also dates the models
that work for VandM.

226
00:11:52,379 --> 00:11:54,009
You're telling me.

227
00:11:54,089 --> 00:11:55,669
Poor Marce!

228
00:11:56,300 --> 00:11:58,840
She's been through so much
because of his infidelities.

229
00:11:59,219 --> 00:12:04,019
Today she thought Armando
had locked himself in a restroom

230
00:12:04,099 --> 00:12:05,729
with one of the models.

231
00:12:05,809 --> 00:12:07,439
Really? Who?

232
00:12:07,937 --> 00:12:09,607
The same one as last year.

233
00:12:09,688 --> 00:12:11,608
The one that caused
the social media scandal.

234
00:12:17,905 --> 00:12:19,865
But that man could be anyone.

235
00:12:24,370 --> 00:12:28,290
Oh, I don't know.
Marce swears it's Armando.

236
00:12:29,416 --> 00:12:32,376
Naomi Ferretti is a menace.

237
00:12:32,461 --> 00:12:34,421
Why else would Marce bar her from VandM?

238
00:12:35,506 --> 00:12:37,926
Those two are mortal enemies.

239
00:12:41,595 --> 00:12:45,265
Patricia, you'll answer the phone,
welcome guests,

240
00:12:45,349 --> 00:12:48,099
take them to the conference room,
handle the catering

241
00:12:48,185 --> 00:12:49,185
and deliver my mail.

242
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:51,979
Yes, I know how to do all that very well.

243
00:12:52,064 --> 00:12:55,284
Beatriz, you'll be my voice
within the company.

244
00:12:55,734 --> 00:12:57,654
You'll speak to the accountants,
administrators,

245
00:12:57,736 --> 00:12:59,146
and handle all fiscal affairs.

246
00:12:59,822 --> 00:13:00,782
Yes.

247
00:13:01,865 --> 00:13:04,785
Sorry, Armand,
but I think you're forgetting

248
00:13:04,868 --> 00:13:08,248
that I studied finance
for three semesters at TUI.

249
00:13:08,455 --> 00:13:09,415
Oh, yes.

250
00:13:09,498 --> 00:13:12,578
First, prove you're capable of handling
everything I asked of you.

251
00:13:12,668 --> 00:13:15,168
Or did you want to take over
Betty's tasks, as well?

252
00:13:15,254 --> 00:13:19,934
Betty, I'll also want reports
on our bank accounts and suppliers.

253
00:13:20,009 --> 00:13:23,259
I'll remind both of you
that you're on a probationary period.

254
00:13:24,346 --> 00:13:29,016
OK, so I'm going to need your passwords.

255
00:13:29,101 --> 00:13:34,271
The ones for your electronic
devices, cell phone, laptop...

256
00:13:34,356 --> 00:13:36,146
so I can manage your agenda.

257
00:13:36,233 --> 00:13:38,323
That's not your job.

258
00:13:38,777 --> 00:13:41,067
Beatriz, you'll manage my personal agenda.

259
00:13:41,488 --> 00:13:42,568
-But...
-No buts.

260
00:13:42,656 --> 00:13:45,866
I don't want to hear your voice
unless it's to transfer a call.

261
00:13:45,951 --> 00:13:49,081
Get to work, you two.
Your desk is outside, Patricia.

262
00:13:50,497 --> 00:13:51,497
Over there?

263
00:13:51,582 --> 00:13:53,252
Yes, out there.

264
00:13:59,256 --> 00:14:00,626
Beatriz, hang back a moment

265
00:14:01,884 --> 00:14:04,054
so I can show you where you'll be working.

266
00:14:15,230 --> 00:14:16,190
Thank you.

267
00:14:19,234 --> 00:14:21,364
Marce! Marce!

268
00:14:21,445 --> 00:14:23,485
What's the matter? What's wrong?

269
00:14:23,572 --> 00:14:26,122
Your fiancé is so annoying!

270
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:28,910
He put that hideous monster above me.

271
00:14:28,994 --> 00:14:34,424
He kept her in his office
and kicked me out.

272
00:14:35,376 --> 00:14:37,206
Here's a word of advice.

273
00:14:37,503 --> 00:14:39,303
Today's your first day on the job.

274
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:41,970
Quit complaining and smile.

275
00:14:44,093 --> 00:14:48,813
Quit complaining and smile?
Perfect, Marcela!

276
00:14:49,681 --> 00:14:53,941
Let me tell you about my job description.

277
00:14:54,812 --> 00:15:01,442
I'm going to answer the phone,
answer emails and serve coffee.

278
00:15:02,152 --> 00:15:04,242
While in the meantime, that mustached uggo

279
00:15:04,321 --> 00:15:08,081
gets to know all of Armando's passwords.

280
00:15:08,158 --> 00:15:09,828
She's going to manage his personal agenda.

281
00:15:11,829 --> 00:15:12,829
She is?

282
00:15:12,913 --> 00:15:15,253
She's going to cover for him.

283
00:15:16,333 --> 00:15:17,253
It's all good, though.

284
00:15:17,334 --> 00:15:20,504
I'll smile and won't complain one bit.

285
00:15:20,587 --> 00:15:24,377
Everything's perfect
in this clueless office.

286
00:15:26,677 --> 00:15:27,547
Come in.

287
00:15:29,179 --> 00:15:30,809
This is it.

288
00:15:30,889 --> 00:15:35,099
I know it's not great,
but this is the only space available.

289
00:15:35,477 --> 00:15:37,557
I wasn't planning
on hiring two secretaries.

290
00:15:37,646 --> 00:15:38,476
Come in.

291
00:15:38,564 --> 00:15:39,484
Thank you.

292
00:15:40,732 --> 00:15:42,402
If you're not comfortable here,

293
00:15:42,484 --> 00:15:45,454
I'll assign you a spot in
the production or design area.

294
00:15:45,529 --> 00:15:47,819
No, don't worry. This is fine.

295
00:15:47,906 --> 00:15:50,906
It's best to stay close
so we can communicate directly.

296
00:15:50,993 --> 00:15:54,083
Sure. I read in your résumé

297
00:15:54,163 --> 00:15:56,873
that you're a very good financial analyst.

298
00:15:56,957 --> 00:15:57,957
Here.

299
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:00,920
This is the business plan
I presented at the meeting.

300
00:16:01,837 --> 00:16:04,007
What do you want me to do with it?

301
00:16:04,089 --> 00:16:06,679
I want a finance expert to analyze it.

302
00:16:06,758 --> 00:16:09,088
Give me your honest opinion.

303
00:16:09,178 --> 00:16:11,348
Sure. Of course. It'd be my pleasure.

304
00:16:13,682 --> 00:16:16,482
I also wanted to thank you
for what you did for me.

305
00:16:18,020 --> 00:16:19,190
In the restroom.

306
00:16:20,898 --> 00:16:23,228
I really appreciate your loyalty.

307
00:16:26,612 --> 00:16:27,492
Armando!

308
00:16:28,739 --> 00:16:29,619
Excuse me.

309
00:16:30,365 --> 00:16:33,235
Why can't Patricia manage your agenda?

310
00:16:33,702 --> 00:16:37,002
Because I don't want her to. Beatriz will.

311
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:40,830
You'd rather let a complete stranger

312
00:16:40,918 --> 00:16:42,838
manage your personal information?

313
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:45,960
Someone so insignificant
and with such poor taste

314
00:16:46,048 --> 00:16:48,008
is going to plan
a fashion company's events?

315
00:16:48,091 --> 00:16:49,051
-Stop!
-What?

316
00:16:49,134 --> 00:16:51,224
-Lower your voice!
-It's the truth.

317
00:16:51,303 --> 00:16:52,933
It's not Beatriz that's bothering you.

318
00:16:53,013 --> 00:16:56,773
You're annoyed
I didn't give your friend access

319
00:16:56,850 --> 00:16:58,350
-to my personal life.
-Nonsense.

320
00:16:58,435 --> 00:17:00,305
-You are.
-And what if I were?

321
00:17:00,395 --> 00:17:01,895
-Do you have anything to hide?
-No.

322
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:05,690
You promised you'd change
when you proposed

323
00:17:05,776 --> 00:17:08,066
and that I'd never have to worry
about you cheating.

324
00:17:08,153 --> 00:17:12,453
And last night you said
you'd make an effort

325
00:17:12,533 --> 00:17:14,833
to trust me more.

326
00:17:14,952 --> 00:17:16,292
What happened to that?

327
00:17:17,287 --> 00:17:20,997
Beatriz will manage my agenda
whether you like it or not.

328
00:17:21,083 --> 00:17:23,843
I just hope she's not
one of your co-conspirators.

329
00:17:23,919 --> 00:17:26,509
If I find out Beatriz is covering for you,

330
00:17:26,588 --> 00:17:29,338
I'll fire her on the spot.

331
00:17:29,424 --> 00:17:30,594
OK.

332
00:17:48,318 --> 00:17:49,488
Hello.

333
00:17:50,487 --> 00:17:53,237
Do any of you know
where I can heat up my food?

334
00:17:53,865 --> 00:17:57,075
In the break room.

335
00:17:57,327 --> 00:17:59,077
But since today's your first day,

336
00:17:59,162 --> 00:18:03,212
the Squad would like to invite you
to have lunch with us.

337
00:18:03,709 --> 00:18:06,339
Thanks, but my mom packed my lunch.

338
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:10,510
I said "invite" because
we all bring our lunch

339
00:18:10,591 --> 00:18:12,551
and eat it together.
It's tastier that way.

340
00:18:13,302 --> 00:18:19,562
We want to spend time with you
and welcome you to VandM.

341
00:18:19,641 --> 00:18:24,101
And we also want to know
why there are two secretaries.

342
00:18:24,396 --> 00:18:25,766
That's never happened before.

343
00:18:25,856 --> 00:18:26,856
Hold on.

344
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:29,940
We don't even know
if she wants to be our friend.

345
00:18:30,027 --> 00:18:31,447
I do.

346
00:18:31,528 --> 00:18:32,898
Yeah!

347
00:18:33,322 --> 00:18:34,572
I'm Betty. Hello.

348
00:18:34,990 --> 00:18:36,830
Nice to meet you. I'm Bertha.

349
00:18:37,242 --> 00:18:38,582
I'm Sofia.

350
00:18:39,202 --> 00:18:41,462
Hi, Betty. I'm Aura Maria.

351
00:18:41,538 --> 00:18:42,498
Sandra.

352
00:18:46,126 --> 00:18:48,166
And I'm Mariana. Nice to meet you.

353
00:18:48,253 --> 00:18:50,093
It's very nice to meet all of you.

354
00:18:51,006 --> 00:18:55,796
Hello. We're going to lunch.

355
00:18:55,886 --> 00:18:58,886
You're welcome to join us
so we can get to know each other.

356
00:19:03,185 --> 00:19:05,305
You're so funny.

357
00:19:05,395 --> 00:19:09,225
Why would I want to get to know you?

358
00:19:16,406 --> 00:19:18,486
She's so funny.

359
00:19:21,870 --> 00:19:22,950
Why are you laughing?

360
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:25,460
What do you mean, Marce?

361
00:19:25,874 --> 00:19:29,174
These girls are so out of touch.

362
00:19:29,252 --> 00:19:32,052
I told you that if you made me
a secretary,

363
00:19:32,130 --> 00:19:34,550
they'd think I was one of them.

364
00:19:34,633 --> 00:19:36,763
-Shall we go have lunch?
-Yes, please!

365
00:19:42,391 --> 00:19:46,191
Hey... so why do you
call yourselves the Squad?

366
00:19:46,269 --> 00:19:48,059
Oh, I can tell you why.

367
00:19:48,146 --> 00:19:52,526
Mr. Hugo Lombardi gave us
the nickname the Ugly Battalion.

368
00:19:52,901 --> 00:19:59,201
We renamed ourselves
the Unconventional Beauties Squad.

369
00:19:59,408 --> 00:20:02,118
Beauty is relative, isn't it?

370
00:20:03,161 --> 00:20:08,041
As you can see, we're all smart,
pretty, and hot.

371
00:20:09,376 --> 00:20:13,626
People say the perfect woman
should be 36-24-36,

372
00:20:13,714 --> 00:20:16,724
but even if some of us
are 36-24-infinity...

373
00:20:17,759 --> 00:20:19,089
Not all of us!

374
00:20:19,177 --> 00:20:21,427
But we're still amazing!

375
00:20:25,308 --> 00:20:28,848
Betty, we have a question.

376
00:20:28,937 --> 00:20:35,027
Since our dear
and charming friend Patricia

377
00:20:35,777 --> 00:20:38,237
is going to be working
at Carmencita's desk,

378
00:20:38,321 --> 00:20:39,781
where will you be working?

379
00:20:39,865 --> 00:20:42,445
In the office right next
to the president's office.

380
00:20:43,034 --> 00:20:43,874
Oh!

381
00:20:43,952 --> 00:20:45,792
What? No!

382
00:20:46,204 --> 00:20:47,584
No, no!

383
00:20:47,664 --> 00:20:50,464
You're working in that dump? No way!

384
00:20:50,542 --> 00:20:57,052
You're definitely one of us.
Welcome to VandM and the Squad.

385
00:20:58,633 --> 00:21:02,053
Welcome! Betty, I have a question.

386
00:21:02,137 --> 00:21:04,637
Did your boss tell you
when he plans to get married?

387
00:21:05,682 --> 00:21:09,772
That hunk is a true alpha male.

388
00:21:09,853 --> 00:21:12,813
Did you hear about the scandal
of the blacklisted model?

389
00:21:12,898 --> 00:21:14,068
-Yes.
-Yeah?

390
00:21:14,149 --> 00:21:15,279
No, no.

391
00:21:15,358 --> 00:21:16,568
-You didn't?
-No.

392
00:21:16,651 --> 00:21:18,491
-Did you or did you not?
-No.

393
00:21:18,570 --> 00:21:19,700
-Want me to fill you in?
-Yeah.

394
00:21:19,780 --> 00:21:22,570
I'm up to speed on everything.

395
00:21:22,657 --> 00:21:28,207
It seems Marcela hates a model
by the name of Naomi Ferretti.

396
00:21:28,330 --> 00:21:30,120
Her name cannot be spoken.

397
00:21:30,207 --> 00:21:32,707
But an error was made
during the hiring process.

398
00:21:38,673 --> 00:21:39,723
Naomi?

399
00:21:42,177 --> 00:21:43,927
Come closer. I've been expecting you.

400
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:46,810
I asked you to meet me here.

401
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:48,810
My agent said I was--

402
00:21:48,892 --> 00:21:51,392
Going to a job?
I'm paying you for your time.

403
00:21:54,523 --> 00:21:57,613
This is what you'd earn in a day
during Fashion Week.

404
00:21:58,193 --> 00:22:01,783
It's a pleasure to meet you.
Daniel Valencia.

405
00:22:01,863 --> 00:22:03,113
-Valencia?
-Uh-huh.

406
00:22:03,198 --> 00:22:05,328
-As in Valencia from VandM?
-Yes, that's right.

407
00:22:05,408 --> 00:22:07,698
I can't believe Marcela
would stoop so low.

408
00:22:07,786 --> 00:22:09,866
Hey, hey. Calm down.

409
00:22:09,955 --> 00:22:11,075
Marcela didn't send me.

410
00:22:11,873 --> 00:22:12,713
I sought you out

411
00:22:12,791 --> 00:22:14,881
because I don't want her
to marry Armando Mendoza.

412
00:22:15,836 --> 00:22:18,046
And if I'm not mistaken, you don't either.

413
00:22:19,422 --> 00:22:21,132
Armando is lying to my sister,

414
00:22:21,508 --> 00:22:24,678
and I need you to tell me
the nature of your relationship.

415
00:22:25,345 --> 00:22:26,175
That's all.

416
00:22:26,263 --> 00:22:29,023
I'm a model, not an informant,
Mr. Valencia.

417
00:22:29,641 --> 00:22:31,521
All right. Here's what we'll do.

418
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:42,528
Naomi, you and I can stop Armando Mendoza.

419
00:22:43,113 --> 00:22:44,113
Think about it.

420
00:22:49,578 --> 00:22:52,208
You have the passwords
to all of my devices.

421
00:22:52,289 --> 00:22:56,879
Please be very discreet.
No one can know those.

422
00:22:57,085 --> 00:22:58,415
Not even Marcela.

423
00:22:58,503 --> 00:22:59,553
Don't worry.

424
00:22:59,629 --> 00:23:02,839
I'm keeping them
in my password manager app.

425
00:23:02,924 --> 00:23:06,854
They'll have to pry that information
from my cold dead hands.

426
00:23:07,804 --> 00:23:10,104
I'm not kidding. This is serious.

427
00:23:10,181 --> 00:23:11,351
Sorry, sir.

428
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:14,733
Everyone here is doing everything they can

429
00:23:14,811 --> 00:23:17,021
to make sure the show is perfect.

430
00:23:20,442 --> 00:23:23,322
This is why it's so important
that you manage my information.

431
00:23:23,486 --> 00:23:24,316
Yeah.

432
00:23:25,113 --> 00:23:29,833
I'm getting married,
and I'm changing my ways.

433
00:23:29,909 --> 00:23:31,869
I really want to be a better man.

434
00:23:32,871 --> 00:23:33,911
So...

435
00:23:34,497 --> 00:23:36,167
<i>Baby, I'm at Le Blanc.</i>

436
00:23:36,249 --> 00:23:38,209
<i>If you don't show up in half an hour,</i>

437
00:23:38,293 --> 00:23:39,883
<i>I'll go looking for you at the office.</i>

438
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:41,500
I have to go.

439
00:23:42,172 --> 00:23:44,262
Go to the office and tell everyone

440
00:23:44,341 --> 00:23:46,891
I'm meeting with O'Brian
from Sportification.

441
00:23:47,427 --> 00:23:49,177
Understood. I'm at your service.

442
00:23:49,262 --> 00:23:50,102
Yes.

443
00:23:53,266 --> 00:23:55,186
-No!
-It's a secret.

444
00:23:55,268 --> 00:23:57,898
Sorry, sorry. I have what you requested.

445
00:23:57,979 --> 00:23:59,939
We wasted a lot of time
because of you, child.

446
00:24:00,023 --> 00:24:02,693
The world moved on, and we did, too.

447
00:24:02,776 --> 00:24:05,606
Where's Armando?
He's not answering my calls.

448
00:24:06,196 --> 00:24:09,656
Mr. Armando had a bit of a problem
with his agenda.

449
00:24:09,741 --> 00:24:10,581
It's just that--

450
00:24:10,659 --> 00:24:12,949
It's just that If I were
managing his schedule,

451
00:24:13,036 --> 00:24:14,536
everything would be
running like clockwork.

452
00:24:15,205 --> 00:24:18,285
When I was at TUI University,

453
00:24:18,541 --> 00:24:25,511
I was a whiz at advanced
organizational patterns.

454
00:24:25,715 --> 00:24:27,505
NASA uses that technology, too.

455
00:24:28,343 --> 00:24:31,393
-That's not it.
-Back talking, too?

456
00:24:31,471 --> 00:24:35,731
Tell me, has a spacecraft ever been late
when landing on the moon?

457
00:24:36,351 --> 00:24:39,151
Kid, we just want to know
why Mr. Armando Mendoza

458
00:24:39,562 --> 00:24:41,482
isn't here meeting with us?

459
00:24:41,564 --> 00:24:44,034
I'm trying to tell you,
but you're not letting me.

460
00:24:44,109 --> 00:24:46,529
-What?
-Sorry, sorry.

461
00:24:47,112 --> 00:24:51,492
Mr. Armando received
an urgent call from Mr. O'Brian,

462
00:24:51,574 --> 00:24:54,914
from Sportification,
and they're meeting about work.

463
00:24:55,286 --> 00:24:58,456
Beatriz, what are you hiding from us?

464
00:24:59,332 --> 00:25:00,172
Nothing.

465
00:25:00,917 --> 00:25:01,877
Nothing?

466
00:25:02,794 --> 00:25:03,804
-No.
-No?

467
00:25:05,130 --> 00:25:08,880
Mr. O'Brian is on vacation.

468
00:25:08,967 --> 00:25:10,507
Oops!

469
00:25:10,969 --> 00:25:12,299
Busted!

470
00:25:15,598 --> 00:25:19,438
Beatriz, tell me where Armando is.

471
00:25:21,104 --> 00:25:24,194
It's over, Naomi.
And this time, I mean it.

472
00:25:25,984 --> 00:25:29,074
No, Armando.
It'll never be over between us.

473
00:25:29,738 --> 00:25:30,858
Come closer.

474
00:25:32,449 --> 00:25:34,329
That's what I like about us.

475
00:25:34,617 --> 00:25:36,487
We make no promises,

476
00:25:36,578 --> 00:25:37,868
and we've lasted longer than most couples.

477
00:25:38,413 --> 00:25:41,673
Listen, you're out of your mind.

478
00:25:42,167 --> 00:25:46,167
I'm going to marry Marcela,
and she's the only woman for me.

479
00:25:46,254 --> 00:25:51,384
Oh, please! You're a terrible liar.

480
00:25:52,761 --> 00:25:54,431
If it were someone else, I'd believe you.

481
00:25:54,721 --> 00:25:55,811
Marcela?

482
00:25:55,889 --> 00:25:58,179
All of Manhattan knows
she's just a business decision for you.

483
00:26:00,101 --> 00:26:01,901
You're free to think whatever you want,

484
00:26:01,978 --> 00:26:05,058
but please don't seek me out again.

485
00:26:06,024 --> 00:26:07,154
And if I refuse?

486
00:26:07,484 --> 00:26:11,574
I'll have to treat you like what you are.

487
00:26:12,363 --> 00:26:13,453
A lunatic.

488
00:26:14,365 --> 00:26:15,445
A lunatic?

489
00:26:16,826 --> 00:26:18,286
You wouldn't.

490
00:26:19,370 --> 00:26:20,710
It'd be a scandal.

491
00:26:20,789 --> 00:26:21,619
All right.

492
00:26:21,706 --> 00:26:22,866
This isn't over. Get back here.

493
00:26:22,957 --> 00:26:24,247
-Armando.
-Margot!

494
00:26:24,334 --> 00:26:25,384
How are you?

495
00:26:25,460 --> 00:26:26,500
I'm well. Thank you.

496
00:26:26,586 --> 00:26:27,496
I heard you're getting married.

497
00:26:27,587 --> 00:26:28,917
-I am.
-Congratulations.

498
00:26:29,005 --> 00:26:31,795
-Thank you.
-Is Marcela with you?

499
00:26:31,883 --> 00:26:34,013
She should be here soon.

500
00:26:34,093 --> 00:26:37,893
I'm in a rush, so I won't get
to congratulate her in person,

501
00:26:37,972 --> 00:26:39,892
but please say hi to her for me.

502
00:26:39,974 --> 00:26:41,314
-Sure.
-It was nice seeing you.

503
00:26:41,392 --> 00:26:42,692
Likewise. Bye.

504
00:26:44,521 --> 00:26:47,941
Don't seek me out again.

505
00:26:48,024 --> 00:26:49,694
If you do, I'll call the police

506
00:26:49,776 --> 00:26:52,446
and file a restraining order against you.

507
00:26:52,529 --> 00:26:53,569
End of story.

508
00:26:54,656 --> 00:26:55,776
Excuse me.

509
00:26:55,865 --> 00:26:56,775
Yes, Beatriz?

510
00:26:56,866 --> 00:26:58,196
Something very serious happened, sir.

511
00:26:58,284 --> 00:27:00,704
<i>Ms. Marcela says Mr. O'Brian is traveling,</i>

512
00:27:00,787 --> 00:27:02,497
and she demands to speak with you.

513
00:27:03,581 --> 00:27:05,421
I'll call the office in five minutes.

514
00:27:05,500 --> 00:27:06,880
I need to come up with an excuse.

515
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:10,460
OK, but please hurry. She's furious!

516
00:27:12,590 --> 00:27:14,930
Beatriz, did you get a hold of Armando?

517
00:27:15,009 --> 00:27:16,639
I'm on it!

518
00:27:29,899 --> 00:27:30,899
Daniel Valencia?

519
00:28:47,143 --> 00:28:51,653
Marce, let Armando speak first,
so he'll dig his own grave.

520
00:28:51,731 --> 00:28:52,821
Of course not!

521
00:28:52,899 --> 00:28:58,319
Men love to say "I love you"
to get you to fall for it.

522
00:29:10,333 --> 00:29:13,003
M-M-Miss M-M-Marcela...

523
00:29:13,878 --> 00:29:15,838
I spoke with Mr. Armando.

524
00:29:16,506 --> 00:29:17,666
The connection wasn't great

525
00:29:17,757 --> 00:29:19,257
so I couldn't make out what he was saying,

526
00:29:19,342 --> 00:29:21,092
but he said he'd call you soon.

527
00:29:21,177 --> 00:29:22,757
Lies upon lies.

528
00:29:27,392 --> 00:29:28,982
Was he with Mr. O'Brian?

529
00:29:31,521 --> 00:29:32,941
Y-y-yes.

530
00:29:34,941 --> 00:29:38,901
Then we'll call him
and he'll put Armando on the line.

531
00:29:52,834 --> 00:29:53,964
<i>How are you?</i>

532
00:29:54,043 --> 00:29:56,593
I'm well. I'm sorry to bother you,

533
00:29:56,671 --> 00:29:59,921
but I heard you had a last-minute meeting
with Armando.

534
00:30:00,008 --> 00:30:01,008
Is everything OK?

535
00:30:16,691 --> 00:30:20,031
Is everything OK
with the company, with life?

536
00:30:41,341 --> 00:30:42,681
I owe you one!

537
00:30:47,013 --> 00:30:49,063
-Ladykillers!
-Ladykillers!

538
00:30:58,733 --> 00:31:01,073
How was your first day on the job, Betty?

539
00:31:03,654 --> 00:31:04,864
Really bad.

540
00:31:05,615 --> 00:31:08,985
Mr. Armando asked me to cover
for him again and I did.

541
00:31:09,452 --> 00:31:12,412
I know I can be so much more
than a secretary.

542
00:31:12,497 --> 00:31:14,167
I can offer the company so much more.

543
00:31:14,248 --> 00:31:16,578
Oh, yeah? Like what?

544
00:31:19,712 --> 00:31:24,472
This is the business plan Mr. Armando
presented to win the presidency.

545
00:31:25,968 --> 00:31:28,758
There are a few mistakes,
but they can be corrected.

546
00:31:29,639 --> 00:31:33,889
I went through it,
and I'll make some suggestions.

547
00:31:34,894 --> 00:31:39,614
And you're making a little extra
for doing this?

548
00:31:39,899 --> 00:31:40,899
No.

549
00:31:41,109 --> 00:31:42,989
That's not why I'm doing it, though.

550
00:31:43,069 --> 00:31:45,819
I want Mr. Armando to know
that he can trust me.

551
00:31:46,197 --> 00:31:47,947
He needs a right-hand person.

552
00:31:48,866 --> 00:31:50,116
What if he's a lefty?

553
00:31:56,374 --> 00:31:58,044
Then I'll be his left-hand person.

554
00:31:58,626 --> 00:32:01,666
I want him to know he can trust me.

555
00:32:01,838 --> 00:32:03,258
A company president needs a right hand.

556
00:32:03,339 --> 00:32:04,419
They're indispensable.

557
00:32:09,095 --> 00:32:10,385
You were checking up on me, weren't you?

558
00:32:10,471 --> 00:32:11,931
Why else would you call O'Brian?

559
00:32:12,014 --> 00:32:14,434
Because I thought
he was still on vacation.

560
00:32:15,685 --> 00:32:17,845
I had my assistant give you a message,

561
00:32:17,937 --> 00:32:19,477
and you didn't believe either of us.

562
00:32:19,689 --> 00:32:21,729
We've had a lot of problems

563
00:32:22,191 --> 00:32:24,531
because you've lied to me about women.

564
00:32:24,610 --> 00:32:26,610
-That's not true.
-Yes, it is!

565
00:32:28,990 --> 00:32:33,040
If going to a meeting leads to this mess,

566
00:32:33,327 --> 00:32:34,997
what will the future hold for us?

567
00:32:35,496 --> 00:32:38,956
Do I have to inform you
of every move I make?

568
00:32:41,961 --> 00:32:45,131
OK. I'm sorry, OK?

569
00:32:45,965 --> 00:32:48,835
I'm under a lot of pressure,
and you're not helping.

570
00:32:50,011 --> 00:32:54,471
I have to answer to my family,
I have to oversee the business

571
00:32:54,557 --> 00:32:56,977
and plan the wedding.

572
00:32:57,435 --> 00:33:01,435
I swear I will.
It'll be this year, I promise.

573
00:33:03,065 --> 00:33:06,145
-Know what would be nice?
-What?

574
00:33:06,235 --> 00:33:10,105
If you announced our engagement
at your dad's going away party.

575
00:33:11,866 --> 00:33:14,536
What? Do you regret it?

576
00:33:14,619 --> 00:33:16,329
No, of course not.

577
00:33:16,412 --> 00:33:18,042
I just want you to know that I love you.

578
00:33:18,789 --> 00:33:19,999
And don't you forget it.

579
00:33:27,924 --> 00:33:29,434
You think Naomi will leave you alone?

580
00:33:30,259 --> 00:33:32,549
She can get upset or get over it.

581
00:33:34,931 --> 00:33:36,521
Hello, Mr. Armando.

582
00:33:36,599 --> 00:33:37,979
Hi, Betty. Good morning.

583
00:33:38,059 --> 00:33:39,479
Let me introduce you.

584
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:42,360
This is Beatriz Rincon,
my personal assistant.

585
00:33:42,438 --> 00:33:45,148
Ricardo Calderon,
VP of Business Management

586
00:33:45,233 --> 00:33:46,283
and minority shareholder.

587
00:33:46,359 --> 00:33:50,199
He's also a friend.
I trust him wholeheartedly.

588
00:33:50,821 --> 00:33:52,451
Nice to meet you, Mr. Ricardo.

589
00:33:53,324 --> 00:33:54,494
Personal assistant?

590
00:33:55,660 --> 00:33:56,870
The pleasure is all mine.

591
00:33:56,953 --> 00:33:58,623
Well, I'll be in my cubicle.

592
00:33:58,704 --> 00:33:59,544
OK.

593
00:34:04,001 --> 00:34:05,881
You're keeping her in the storage room?

594
00:34:05,962 --> 00:34:07,802
I had to put her somewhere.
Where else would she go?

595
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:09,590
Outside, with the rest of the gargoyles!

596
00:34:10,758 --> 00:34:11,628
She's very efficient.

597
00:34:11,717 --> 00:34:13,837
At getting rid of evil spirits.

598
00:34:18,432 --> 00:34:20,312
Please think this through.

599
00:34:21,686 --> 00:34:25,516
If you agree to do this,
it'll be harder to leave Marcela.

600
00:34:27,316 --> 00:34:29,026
I already planned the after-party.

601
00:34:29,110 --> 00:34:31,570
You have no idea how many babes
are coming.

602
00:34:31,654 --> 00:34:33,244
All right, I'll just say one thing.

603
00:34:33,322 --> 00:34:35,742
Do you really have to make
the announcement today?

604
00:34:35,825 --> 00:34:36,735
Yes. It's happening.

605
00:34:39,579 --> 00:34:41,499
I can't believe it. We should be mourning.

606
00:34:41,581 --> 00:34:44,291
Do you think I can handle
that after-party by myself?

607
00:34:44,375 --> 00:34:46,245
Shut up. Here they come.

608
00:34:46,544 --> 00:34:49,514
You can do it tomorrow.
It doesn't have to be today.

609
00:34:49,589 --> 00:34:50,719
Zip it.

610
00:34:51,090 --> 00:34:52,970
Auntie, you look beautiful, as always.

611
00:34:53,050 --> 00:34:55,720
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

612
00:34:55,803 --> 00:34:56,973
Hi.

613
00:34:57,054 --> 00:34:57,894
-Uncle.
-Hi.

614
00:34:57,972 --> 00:34:59,932
-Today's the today.
-This all looks great.

615
00:35:00,016 --> 00:35:01,596
-We are so proud of you.
-Thank you.

616
00:35:01,851 --> 00:35:04,941
Let's hope this isn't VandM's
last big runway show.

617
00:35:05,730 --> 00:35:08,940
Always the well-wisher.

618
00:35:09,400 --> 00:35:11,240
But I'll remind you
that this is your company, too.

619
00:35:11,319 --> 00:35:12,989
You'd benefit from us doing well.

620
00:35:13,070 --> 00:35:15,570
And I'll remind you
that both of our families' fortunes

621
00:35:15,656 --> 00:35:16,486
are in your hands.

622
00:35:16,574 --> 00:35:18,584
I'll remind both of you of where we are.

623
00:35:19,201 --> 00:35:21,581
Behave accordingly. Like adults!

624
00:35:21,662 --> 00:35:23,002
I agree.

625
00:35:23,289 --> 00:35:26,419
Dani, let's get a drink and mingle.

626
00:35:28,419 --> 00:35:30,209
I have to greet some important people.

627
00:35:36,927 --> 00:35:38,217
OK.

628
00:35:41,599 --> 00:35:46,149
Roberto, Margarita,
when I look at you, my eyes water.

629
00:35:46,604 --> 00:35:48,064
We're really going to miss you very much.

630
00:35:48,147 --> 00:35:49,727
Your absence will be felt.

631
00:35:49,815 --> 00:35:54,565
You have no idea what your son
has planned for VandM.

632
00:35:54,654 --> 00:35:57,284
We're working on a new casual,
ready-to-wear line.

633
00:35:58,532 --> 00:36:00,992
My line sheet! Your dad has to see it.

634
00:36:01,077 --> 00:36:03,537
I don't have it with me.
It's in my office.

635
00:36:03,621 --> 00:36:05,581
Don't worry, though.
I'll have it brought over.

636
00:36:10,461 --> 00:36:11,341
Betty.

637
00:36:13,673 --> 00:36:15,343
The taxi will be here soon.

638
00:36:15,925 --> 00:36:17,085
This is so exciting.

639
00:36:17,218 --> 00:36:19,138
I'd love to attend an event like that.

640
00:36:19,553 --> 00:36:22,643
I bet there are lots
of beautiful, elegant people

641
00:36:22,723 --> 00:36:25,063
and so many hot men.

642
00:36:26,352 --> 00:36:27,852
You can come with me if you like.

643
00:36:27,937 --> 00:36:29,357
-Sure.
-We can't.

644
00:36:29,980 --> 00:36:31,770
Only executives are allowed.

645
00:36:31,857 --> 00:36:35,607
Mariana gets to go because she handles
the social media stuff.

646
00:36:36,070 --> 00:36:38,200
We don't. That sucks.

647
00:36:38,280 --> 00:36:39,950
It's here. Bye.

648
00:36:40,032 --> 00:36:41,282
Betty, one more thing.

649
00:36:41,367 --> 00:36:43,697
I peeked at the menu,
and everything looks delicious.

650
00:36:43,786 --> 00:36:47,286
If you're allowed to have food,
bring some for us.

651
00:36:47,373 --> 00:36:48,213
Yes, sure.

652
00:36:48,290 --> 00:36:50,420
Don't forget to photograph the hotties.

653
00:36:50,501 --> 00:36:51,671
Send the pictures to our group chat.

654
00:36:51,752 --> 00:36:52,592
OK, bye.

655
00:36:54,922 --> 00:36:57,552
Is your dad coming?

656
00:36:58,134 --> 00:37:00,304
I don't think so.
Too many issues at the office.

657
00:37:00,386 --> 00:37:01,216
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

658
00:37:01,303 --> 00:37:02,263
Hello.

659
00:37:03,180 --> 00:37:04,520
Hi, Roberto.

660
00:37:05,224 --> 00:37:06,684
Congratulations.

661
00:37:06,767 --> 00:37:09,557
You've left your son a wonderful legacy.

662
00:37:11,564 --> 00:37:13,324
I feel good about retiring

663
00:37:13,399 --> 00:37:15,689
because the company is in good hands.

664
00:37:16,318 --> 00:37:20,158
I hope my dad is just as proud
when it's my turn to take over.

665
00:37:20,239 --> 00:37:21,869
He will be. You'll see.

666
00:37:22,324 --> 00:37:23,284
Trust him.

667
00:37:23,367 --> 00:37:25,657
-Tiffany, it's so nice to see you.
-Hi.

668
00:37:25,745 --> 00:37:27,405
I have to steal him away.

669
00:37:27,496 --> 00:37:28,826
You're wanted for an interview.

670
00:37:28,914 --> 00:37:30,584
-Again?
-Come on.

671
00:37:30,666 --> 00:37:32,246
Well, duty calls.

672
00:37:32,334 --> 00:37:33,844
Enjoy.

673
00:37:33,961 --> 00:37:35,211
Thank you.

674
00:37:37,173 --> 00:37:38,593
-Know what I'm going to do?
-What?

675
00:37:38,674 --> 00:37:40,594
I'm going to invite your father
to a game of golf.

676
00:37:41,177 --> 00:37:42,507
He'll be thrilled.

677
00:37:42,636 --> 00:37:44,926
-Yeah?
-Yeah. Of course.

678
00:38:24,762 --> 00:38:26,642
What are you doing there? Get inside!

679
00:38:26,722 --> 00:38:29,182
I'm trying, but the hall monitor
won't let me through.

680
00:38:44,406 --> 00:38:45,906
-Thank you!
-Come on.

681
00:38:46,826 --> 00:38:47,906
Thank you so much.

682
00:38:47,993 --> 00:38:50,663
Mr. Armando asked me to deliver
these to Hugo immediately.

683
00:38:50,746 --> 00:38:52,076
Go on, then. He's waiting for you.

684
00:38:53,165 --> 00:38:54,075
Naomi!

685
00:38:54,166 --> 00:38:56,086
Mr. Armando is a dead man.

686
00:38:56,544 --> 00:38:59,174
No, we can keep Ms. Marcela
from seeing her.

687
00:38:59,255 --> 00:39:03,175
I'll keep her busy, and you keep her
away from Mr. Armando.

688
00:39:48,679 --> 00:39:49,809
Good afternoon, everyone.

689
00:39:49,889 --> 00:39:53,019
Welcome to VandM's new collection launch.

690
00:39:53,100 --> 00:39:55,900
We chose this beautiful set as a backdrop

691
00:39:55,978 --> 00:39:58,108
to honor a man who has dedicated

692
00:39:58,188 --> 00:40:00,728
more than 30 years
to the world of fashion.

693
00:40:01,066 --> 00:40:02,986
My father, Roberto Mendoza.

694
00:40:11,660 --> 00:40:14,710
Welcome all! Enjoy VandM's new collection.

695
00:40:38,979 --> 00:40:39,809
Naomi!

696
00:40:54,870 --> 00:40:56,120
No, no, no!

697
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:01,710
Don't!

698
00:43:38,200 --> 00:43:39,330
What is that woman doing here?

699
00:43:39,868 --> 00:43:41,448
She came to bring Hugo's sketchbook.

700
00:43:41,870 --> 00:43:44,370
-On the runway?
-She was looking for me.

701
00:43:44,456 --> 00:43:47,376
Quit making excuses for her.
She made a mess of everything!

702
00:43:47,459 --> 00:43:48,999
This was a hit!

703
00:43:49,086 --> 00:43:50,336
What are you talking about?

704
00:43:53,549 --> 00:43:56,549
Didn't you see when she threw herself
on the runway?

705
00:43:56,635 --> 00:43:59,175
People are staring. Please smile.

706
00:43:59,263 --> 00:44:00,103
Thanks!

707
00:44:12,317 --> 00:44:13,647
Could I have a moment of your time?

708
00:44:13,735 --> 00:44:14,605
Sure.

709
00:44:17,990 --> 00:44:20,740
What are you doing here?
I said it was over between us.

710
00:44:20,826 --> 00:44:22,156
You were very clear.

711
00:44:22,244 --> 00:44:24,294
I'm here for Marcela, not you.

712
00:44:24,371 --> 00:44:25,461
Don't drag Marcela into this.

713
00:44:25,539 --> 00:44:27,619
You dragged her into this
when you proposed to her.

714
00:44:28,333 --> 00:44:31,423
She deserves to know
the type of man she's marrying.

715
00:44:32,171 --> 00:44:35,011
You want to talk to her and ruin my life?

716
00:44:35,090 --> 00:44:39,220
I'll take you to her so you can
tell her everything about us.

717
00:44:39,303 --> 00:44:41,223
-Come on.
-You think I won't?

718
00:44:41,305 --> 00:44:42,385
Oh, I know you will.

719
00:44:43,182 --> 00:44:45,642
I'll take you to her so you can talk,

720
00:44:45,726 --> 00:44:48,146
and then you can forget
about your modeling career

721
00:44:48,228 --> 00:44:49,938
because I'll call every agency, magazine

722
00:44:50,022 --> 00:44:51,942
and fashion house and you'll never model

723
00:44:52,024 --> 00:44:53,694
so much as oven mitts again!

724
00:44:54,026 --> 00:44:55,276
You're not that powerful.

725
00:44:55,360 --> 00:44:56,650
Try me!

726
00:44:57,863 --> 00:45:01,243
I won't let some lunatic,
some psycho ruin my life.

727
00:45:02,367 --> 00:45:03,827
You're a bastard!

728
00:45:04,202 --> 00:45:07,462
I swear you'll pay for each
and every woman you've hurt.

729
00:45:15,797 --> 00:45:18,507
Stop! Isn't that Naomi?

730
00:45:20,469 --> 00:45:22,639
It is. What is she doing here?

731
00:45:22,721 --> 00:45:24,061
Let's find out.

732
00:45:24,139 --> 00:45:26,309
-Marcelita, darling.
-How are you, Margot?

733
00:45:26,391 --> 00:45:27,731
-Hi, Patricia.
-Hi.

734
00:45:27,809 --> 00:45:29,229
Everything turned out so nice.

735
00:45:29,311 --> 00:45:31,981
Not even that tiny hiccup
could ruin the show.

736
00:45:32,064 --> 00:45:33,524
-Congratulations!
-Thank you!

737
00:45:33,815 --> 00:45:37,355
By the way, I saw Armando
at a restaurant yesterday.

738
00:45:37,444 --> 00:45:38,284
What? Yesterday?

739
00:45:38,362 --> 00:45:39,242
Yes.

740
00:45:39,321 --> 00:45:40,821
-Are you sure it was him?
-Yes.

741
00:45:40,906 --> 00:45:44,276
I asked about you,
and he said you were on your way.

742
00:45:44,368 --> 00:45:46,578
He was with a model that'd worked for you.

743
00:45:46,703 --> 00:45:48,833
What's her name? Noemi?

744
00:45:48,914 --> 00:45:50,044
Naomi.

745
00:45:50,123 --> 00:45:50,963
Yes, her.

746
00:45:52,250 --> 00:45:55,590
Mariana, I ruined Mr. Armando's
first runway show.

747
00:45:55,671 --> 00:45:57,261
I bet he hates me right now.

748
00:45:57,339 --> 00:46:00,179
It was an accident, Betty.

749
00:46:00,258 --> 00:46:02,888
Give it some time
and everyone will have forgotten.

750
00:46:12,354 --> 00:46:13,444
Where is she?

751
00:46:14,314 --> 00:46:17,734
How dare you remain here
after what you did?

752
00:46:17,985 --> 00:46:21,195
Days and nights of work
ruined because of you!

753
00:46:21,530 --> 00:46:23,740
You're a destroyer of aesthetics
and beauty!

754
00:46:23,824 --> 00:46:25,164
What the hell are you doing here?

755
00:46:25,242 --> 00:46:26,912
Sorry, sorry! It was an accident!

756
00:46:26,994 --> 00:46:28,414
Your birth was an accident.

757
00:46:28,495 --> 00:46:31,285
Will removing the hideous rags
you call clothes

758
00:46:31,373 --> 00:46:34,883
and using them to drown you
qualify as an accident, too?

759
00:46:35,210 --> 00:46:38,050
Ugly people should die! Get out!

760
00:46:38,130 --> 00:46:39,590
-Calm down.
-Don't.

761
00:46:39,673 --> 00:46:42,803
You know what I'm like when I'm like this.

762
00:46:42,884 --> 00:46:44,054
Yes, yes...

763
00:46:44,136 --> 00:46:46,636
I'll never set foot... Listen to me.

764
00:46:46,722 --> 00:46:48,272
I'll never set foot in VandM again.

765
00:46:48,348 --> 00:46:49,348
This was my last runway show.

766
00:46:49,641 --> 00:46:51,811
Leave me alone. Give me some space.

767
00:46:51,893 --> 00:46:55,063
Are you deaf? Leave the planet!

768
00:46:55,147 --> 00:46:56,187
Go!

769
00:46:57,024 --> 00:46:58,574
Betty!

770
00:46:59,568 --> 00:47:02,488
You really lucked out.
Had Naomi spoken to Marcela...

771
00:47:03,739 --> 00:47:05,159
Nothing would've happened.

772
00:47:05,240 --> 00:47:06,580
It would've been her word against mine.

773
00:47:06,658 --> 00:47:07,578
-What?
-Yes.

774
00:47:08,243 --> 00:47:10,703
We live in the era of social media.

775
00:47:10,787 --> 00:47:15,957
Never in the history of male infidelity
have we been so...

776
00:47:16,293 --> 00:47:17,343
so watched.

777
00:47:17,753 --> 00:47:18,753
We're cornered.

778
00:47:18,837 --> 00:47:21,207
I've been backed into a corner
due to Betty's mishap.

779
00:47:21,298 --> 00:47:22,838
We're getting off on the wrong foot.

780
00:47:24,342 --> 00:47:26,682
If Betty had been just a little prettier,

781
00:47:26,762 --> 00:47:28,602
it would've been different.

782
00:47:28,680 --> 00:47:30,970
You know people like beauty.

783
00:47:31,475 --> 00:47:34,345
No, that's not it, but I think
hiring her was a mistake.

784
00:47:34,436 --> 00:47:35,766
I'll have to fire her.

785
00:47:35,854 --> 00:47:37,194
-Mr. Armando.
-Not now, Mariana.

786
00:47:37,606 --> 00:47:40,276
I hope Hugo doesn't get
in one of his moods.

787
00:47:40,358 --> 00:47:41,398
-Fat chance!
-Mr. Armando.

788
00:47:41,485 --> 00:47:42,775
Not now! What is it?

789
00:47:42,861 --> 00:47:44,911
I have to talk to you.
It's very important.

790
00:47:44,988 --> 00:47:46,738
-It can't wait.
-What is it?

791
00:48:01,379 --> 00:48:03,129
What do you think you're doing?

792
00:48:04,424 --> 00:48:06,644
Picking up Mr. Hugo's designs.

793
00:48:06,718 --> 00:48:08,798
It's called a line sheet.

794
00:48:09,429 --> 00:48:11,559
You must mean what's left of the work

795
00:48:11,640 --> 00:48:15,770
of one of the company's top designers.

796
00:48:16,394 --> 00:48:18,404
The horror! You're so ugly.

797
00:48:19,272 --> 00:48:21,982
Why don't you quit, Ugly Betty?

798
00:48:22,275 --> 00:48:24,895
No one will want you
at VandM tomorrow anyway.

799
00:48:26,404 --> 00:48:27,284
It was an accident.

800
00:48:27,364 --> 00:48:33,874
Yes, you're an accident.
An accident I'm grateful for.

801
00:48:33,954 --> 00:48:37,004
I'll get to be Armand's assistant now.

802
00:48:38,625 --> 00:48:39,785
Don't be sad.

803
00:48:40,460 --> 00:48:41,550
It's not my fault.

804
00:48:41,628 --> 00:48:45,168
Some people are born to shine

805
00:48:45,257 --> 00:48:48,297
and others, like you, are meant
to watch us shine from below.

806
00:49:16,788 --> 00:49:17,958
Hi, Dad.

807
00:49:18,039 --> 00:49:19,169
Hi, sweetie.

808
00:49:19,666 --> 00:49:20,826
Guess what?

809
00:49:20,917 --> 00:49:23,297
I gave the attorney his retainer.

810
00:49:23,378 --> 00:49:24,378
He's expensive,

811
00:49:24,462 --> 00:49:26,592
but paying his fees will be worth it

812
00:49:26,673 --> 00:49:28,633
now that you're helping me.

813
00:49:29,301 --> 00:49:30,971
How expensive?

814
00:49:32,095 --> 00:49:34,135
Not as expensive as I initially thought.

815
00:49:34,222 --> 00:49:36,352
He advertises his services on TV all day.

816
00:49:36,516 --> 00:49:39,476
I'm feeling very optimistic.

817
00:49:39,811 --> 00:49:41,731
Look! That's him!

818
00:49:41,813 --> 00:49:42,983
That's Peter!

819
00:50:11,509 --> 00:50:13,679
Oh, my. You think he's any good?

820
00:50:13,762 --> 00:50:15,432
Of course he is.

821
00:50:15,513 --> 00:50:17,893
If he weren't, he wouldn't be on TV.

822
00:50:18,516 --> 00:50:21,516
-Yeah.
-What's wrong? You seem down.

823
00:50:21,603 --> 00:50:22,733
Did something happen today?

824
00:50:24,773 --> 00:50:26,363
Just adapting to the new job.

825
00:50:28,026 --> 00:50:31,026
I know the first days are hard.

826
00:50:32,280 --> 00:50:37,490
I went through it when I went
from a janitor in night school

827
00:50:37,577 --> 00:50:39,617
to the office accountant.

828
00:50:41,164 --> 00:50:44,634
But you know what? It'll be OK.

829
00:50:44,709 --> 00:50:47,339
Tomorrow will always be a better day.

830
00:50:47,420 --> 00:50:50,010
Take it from your dad that loves you.

831
00:50:50,090 --> 00:50:51,010
And I you.

832
00:50:52,550 --> 00:50:54,390
Do you watch this series?

833
00:50:57,138 --> 00:51:01,348
I really appreciate your help.

834
00:51:01,851 --> 00:51:05,271
Yes, please be very discreet.

835
00:51:05,355 --> 00:51:07,605
Whatever you want. You're so sweet.

836
00:51:07,691 --> 00:51:08,781
Thank you!

837
00:51:15,156 --> 00:51:18,446
If you didn't want the phone,
you could've given it to me!

838
00:51:18,535 --> 00:51:20,035
He lied to me, Patricia!

839
00:51:20,120 --> 00:51:21,750
He wasn't at a business meeting!

840
00:51:21,830 --> 00:51:23,670
He was with that slut at Le Blanc!

841
00:51:23,748 --> 00:51:26,288
The restaurant manager just confirmed it.

842
00:51:29,838 --> 00:51:35,968
And Uggo was probably covering for him.

843
00:51:36,803 --> 00:51:38,973
That's why she caused that scene
during the fashion show.

844
00:51:39,055 --> 00:51:41,135
So you wouldn't realize Naomi was there.

845
00:51:41,224 --> 00:51:43,064
Shut up! Don't remind me!

846
00:51:43,143 --> 00:51:46,603
Armando forgot to announce
our engagement because of her!

847
00:51:47,147 --> 00:51:49,647
Now I get why Armando hired her.

848
00:51:49,733 --> 00:51:51,943
To be his accomplice!

849
00:51:53,069 --> 00:51:57,699
You poor thing.
They're making a fool of you.

850
00:51:58,533 --> 00:52:00,873
I imagine you're going
to confront Armando.

851
00:52:00,952 --> 00:52:02,502
No, Patricia!

852
00:52:02,579 --> 00:52:04,209
I'll handle the bigger issue here.

853
00:52:11,338 --> 00:52:12,918
Oh!

854
00:52:14,632 --> 00:52:16,892
Don't worry, Mariana. I'll be fine.

855
00:52:18,762 --> 00:52:20,562
I was really worried about you yesterday.

856
00:52:20,638 --> 00:52:23,058
You looked so sad and upset.

857
00:52:23,391 --> 00:52:24,981
Of course I was.

858
00:52:25,143 --> 00:52:29,653
I ruined Mr. Armando's and Hugo's big day.

859
00:52:29,731 --> 00:52:30,611
I bet they hate me right now.

860
00:52:30,690 --> 00:52:32,150
I doubt it.

861
00:52:32,317 --> 00:52:38,027
Mr. Armando can be surly
and a bit of a dictator,

862
00:52:38,114 --> 00:52:40,414
but he's a good person. He'll understand.

863
00:52:41,534 --> 00:52:42,374
But Hugo...

864
00:52:56,633 --> 00:52:58,263
Good morning, Ms. Marcela.

865
00:52:58,343 --> 00:53:00,893
Spare me the greeting
and gather your things.

866
00:53:12,816 --> 00:53:14,436
It was worse.